{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokesEigenvalues","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.transposition_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.transposition_sq","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The monodromy element itself, as a permutation of the three roots: a transposition squares\nto the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_eigen_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_eigen_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L71-L74","doc":"Eigenvector for the eigenvalue `−1` (the antisymmetric channel `L₋` at `q = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_eigen_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_eigen_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L67-L69","doc":"Eigenvector for the eigenvalue `+1` (the symmetric channel `L₊` at `q = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_satisfies_hecke_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_satisfies_hecke_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The swap satisfies the Hecke quadratic at `q = 1`: `S² − (1 − 1⁻¹)S − 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap_sq","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L58-L60","doc":"A transposition is an involution: `S² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.swap","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The swap of the two colliding roots at a simple branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.hecke_quadratic_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.hecke_quadratic_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeQuadraticClassicalShadow.lean#L49-L53","doc":"The Hecke quadratic `X² − (q − q⁻¹)X − 1` at `q = 1` is `(X − 1)(X + 1)`: the minimal\npolynomial of a reflection. (The `q ≠ 0` factorisation `stokes_curvature_factors` specialised.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}